# Pre-existing external redirect. Kept above the rewrites below: Pages takes
# the first match, and this is an exact path that must not fall through.
/submit-music https://deejaytools.com/ 301

# Path-preserving shells for the private note routes.
#
# These pages address a resource by path — /notes/<uuid> — and that is worth
# keeping: a path segment identifies a resource, a query parameter describes a
# page. A static build cannot enumerate them, and must not: the ids are private,
# and putting them in getStaticPaths would publish the id set inside a public
# artifact. So one shell is built per route and rewritten to here, and the shell
# reads the id from location.pathname and fetches it with a credential.
#
# 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the URL in the address bar is unchanged.
#
# Ordering is deepest-first, because Pages takes the first match. Real files
# still win over these rules, which is what keeps /notes/admin, /notes/ask and
# /notes itself resolving to their own pages rather than the shell.
/notes/admin/*   /notes/admin/detail   200
/admin/notes/*   /admin/notes/detail   200
/notes/*         /notes/detail         200
